Week 14 box 3: whole-report layout pass over report/report.pdf (129 pages), 5 November 2026.

Method
- Built with latexmk -pdf (MiKTeX); 0 undefined references or citations.
- Every page rendered at 45 dpi and tiled 8 per sheet (17 sheets); every sheet looked at.
- Every diagram and figure page, and every page the log flagged, rendered again at 55-110 dpi and read:
  pp. 20, 26-30 (ERDs, class diagrams, API and event tables), 33-35 (sequence diagrams), 37 (failure table),
  41 (C1 table), 84, 89-92, 105-115 (Results tables and figures), 116-129 (Discussion to Appendix D).
- Overfull lines from report.log before and after.

Overfull lines in report.log
- before: 35, of which 20 were 10 pt or wider (largest 196 pt: the event table; 102 pt: an evidence path).
- after: 16, of which 2 are 10 pt or wider; both were read at 70 dpi and do not reach the margin
  (p. 20 a description-list label box, p. 37 a p-column of the failure table).

Fixed
- Event table (sec. 10.4): wrapped columns, small type (was 196 pt too wide).
- Local infrastructure table (sec. 9.1): wrapped columns.
- C1 below/equal/above table (p. 41, the known overflow): tighter column spacing.
- 170 file paths, evidence names and metric names moved from \texttt to \nolinkurl, which may now break
  after / - . _ and inside UTC timestamps; long C# identifiers given break points.
- Event-contract sentence (p. 29) reordered so FlashSale.EventContracts no longer runs into the margin.
- Generated Results tables capped at the text width (adjustbox max width).
- ERD figures 10.1-10.3 and the event-contract diagram 10.5: their text printed at about 3-4 pt. The rendered
  images were re-packed from one row into two rows (report/figures/stack_wide.py, *-stacked.png; content
  unchanged, the Mermaid sources untouched) and printed larger, about 1.4 to 2.5 times the earlier text size.
- Appendix D lists the Week 14 evidence (TP-X02, TP-X09 re-freeze, TP-X10, TP-X11, TP-X12); Appendix C points
  to the run plan and the owner steps.

Left as they are, by judgement
- Sequence diagrams 10.7 and 10.8 fill the page height; their text is small but legible when the PDF is zoomed,
  and the full diagrams are in docs/sequence-diagrams.md.
- A few pages are part-empty where a float ends a chapter or section; no table or figure is cut or overflows.

